  "id": "COMPOUND:1031 - PROTEIN:4923",
  "verbalization": "Ibuprofen appears to have a dual relationship with Neuropilin-2, as it is a target of two distinct pathways: one involving Patiromer and another involving 2-cyclohexen-1-one. The first pathway links Ibuprofen to Carnitine O-palmitoyltransferase 1, which is then targeted by Patiromer, ultimately leading to Neuropilin-2. The second pathway connects Ibuprofen to Ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2, which is targeted by 2-cyclohexen-1-one, also leading to Neuropilin-2. These pathways suggest that Ibuprofen may influence Neuropilin-2 through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving enzyme activity or metabolic regulation. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Ibuprofen to modulate Neuropilin-2 through distinct biochemical routes, emphasizing the complexity of its interaction with the nervous system.",
